{
  "_readme": "GAME CONTENT, DRAFT PENDING PRODUCER REVIEW (every DisplayName and story Text; no art yet: ArtKey is a placeholder key). The Board (docs/design/grove.md): destinations unlock from the first save (\"start\") or from a Grove habitat being unlocked (\"habitat\", UnlockId names it) \u2014 not from a discovery.json shrine in v1, since no shrine ids were reserved for destinations and reserving new ones would touch discovery.json's own points-of-interest capacity math, out of this PR's scope; a producer-reviewable trim, see docs/design/grove.md. Sending a party (ExpeditionRules.Send) is a timer on the destination only: the beasts sent stay fully available for battle and idle XP the whole time away (producer decision). Waiting is checked through OfflineClock; collecting (ExpeditionRules.Collect) rolls the destination's OutcomeTables entry with the same seeded-roll-plus-pity idiom as the Grove's gifts: a \"story\" entry unlocks a Stories entry (the codex's future seed), a \"trinket\" entry adds a Grove item, and a \"look\" entry (not authored here yet) would unlock a cosmetic look. Validated by BeastCraft.Expeditions.ExpeditionLibraryValidator (content load and the EditMode tests).",
